# Expanded reference validation plan

Status: implemented_pending_expanded_reference. No new quantum-chemical reference calculation was performed during package development.

## Inspected primary evidence

- paper_main, PDF pages [2, 3, 4]: Scheme1 visually inspected: o-tolyl rather than para-tolyl and benzyl N substituents; full series absorption argument read.
- paper_si, PDF pages [10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24]: CIF compound identity, method and TD tables inspected. Covalent bond loop examined to separate symmetry-related portions of compound2.

## Reusable legacy evidence

Compound2 CIF and chemical formula are reusable private identity provenance. Old excitation mismatch and source/table differences do not calibrate the new four-member matrix. The private legacy_final_snapshot is a byte-for-byte provenance archive, not new completion evidence.

## New reference gaps

Complete series minima, common-core constrained states, N6-resolved matching and expanded uncertainty references remain uncalculated.

## Minimum pilot

Confirm compound2 graph/formula68 total atoms against a symmetry-completed CIF component; run its root window and one substituent control before1–4 expansion.

## Full expanded validation

Execute the complete public matrix, inspect identities and raw outputs, reproduce all new differences and sensitivity analyses, and independently review the claimed discrimination. Calibrate property-specific method/sampling errors before any numerical acceptance bands. Do not reuse narrow legacy tolerances. Document failed, collapsed and unresolved candidates rather than inventing minima.

## Available route and resource boundary

Gaussian/ORCA SMD-DCM DFT/TDDFT; Multiwfn or reproducible NTO/population analysis; CIF parser only for provenance checks. Consult chemistry_toolbox/README.md, config/native_software_manual_profiles.yaml, native_software_docs/gaussian/QUICKSTART.md, orca/EXCITED_STATES.md, crest/CONFORMER_SEARCH.md and goodvibes/QUICKSTART.md as applicable. Listed capabilities are not proof that this expanded system has run. Use inspect_software and validate_native_job before submission. This authoring run did not submit long jobs, HPC work or paid services.
